    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d858">

                <pb facs="0872" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 865.857An2/29b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Austria-Hungary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Penfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-16T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1915, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>987. The Embassy has transmitted a copy of the Austro-Hungarian Admiralty’s
                    official report regarding the sinking of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Ancona</hi>. Please ascertain the size and character of the attacking vessel,
                    its armament, the name of the commander, and the flag flown during the attack.
                    If possible, also obtain a copy of the commander’s report.</p>
                <p>Please examine the list of Austro-Hungarian submarines and report whether the
                    vessel attacking the <hi rendition="#italic">Ancona</hi> appears on the
                    list.</p>
                <p>Report promptly by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
